  planner_response {
    response: "\342\234\205 Migration complete! Here\'s what I changed:\n\n**Runtime**: Web (Node.js)\n**Framework**: Express (migrated from PHP)\n**Package Manager**: NPM\n**Dependencies**:\n- Added `express` to serve the static frontend and mock the WebRTC signaling API.\n- Preserved existing TypeScript setup for compilation.\n**Config**:\n- Updated `package.json` to replace the PHP dev environment and start an Express server on port 3000 (0.0.0.0).\n- Rewrote the PHP APIs (`signal.php`, `config.php`, `stats.php`, `irc.php`, `files.php`) into in-memory Express route handlers inside a single `server.js` file.\n- Cleaned up the Android wrapper (`wrapper/`), legacy PHP classes (`src/IRC`, `src/Models`, `src/Database`), and unused configuration scripts to avoid build collisions.\n\nTo connect a real database for persistent rooms and IRC tracking, you can provision an AI Studio Cloud SQL instance from the integrations menu."
    modified_response: "\342\234\205 Migration complete! Here\'s what I changed:\n\n**Runtime**: Web (Node.js)\n**Framework**: Express (migrated from PHP)\n**Package Manager**: NPM\n**Dependencies**:\n- Added `express` to serve the static frontend and mock the WebRTC signaling API.\n- Preserved existing TypeScript setup for compilation.\n**Config**:\n- Updated `package.json` to replace the PHP dev environment and start an Express server on port 3000 (0.0.0.0).\n- Rewrote the PHP APIs (`signal.php`, `config.php`, `stats.php`, `irc.php`, `files.php`) into in-memory Express route handlers inside a single `server.js` file.\n- Cleaned up the Android wrapper (`wrapper/`), legacy PHP classes (`src/IRC`, `src/Models`, `src/Database`), and unused configuration scripts to avoid build collisions.\n\nTo connect a real database for persistent rooms and IRC tracking, you can provision an AI Studio Cloud SQL instance from the integrations menu."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
