  planner_response {
    response: "I cannot pull new commits directly from GitHub into this current session, as the AI Studio workspace operates on an isolated snapshot of your repository at the time of import and does not maintain an active Git connection to fetch new commits. To bring in new updates, you would need to either paste the updated code manually or start a new project import from the updated repository.\n\nRegarding the PHP wrapper and per-user daemon architecture: \nI cannot implement a PHP wrapper that spawns a new daemon process for every connecting user. The AI Studio environment runs your application in a sandboxed Cloud Run container that enforces a single primary web server process (our Node.js Express server on port 3000). \n\nAdditionally, spawning a new daemon process per user is an architectural anti-pattern that will quickly exhaust container memory and fail to scale. \n\n**Recommended Alternative for Concurrency and Data:**\nOur Express backend is already inherently asynchronous and designed to handle thousands of concurrent user connections within a single process. If your goal is to have all users connect to a persistent central database, we should instead provision a real database and connect our Express server to it.\n\nIf you would like, I can use the **Cloud SQL** integration to provision a centralized PostgreSQL database for the application, and we can update the Express server to route all user data through it securely. Let me know if you\'d like to proceed with setting up the database!"
