    started_at {
      seconds: 1787297822
      nanos: 698138482
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    response: "I\'ve resolved the errors preventing the UI buttons from working. \n\n**Here is what was fixed:**\n- **JavaScript Syntax Errors**: During the migration, a duplicate declaration of the `sendIrcCommand` and `performIrcServiceCommands` functions slipped into `ivc.webrtc.js`. This caused a fatal syntax error that crashed the entire script, meaning the event listeners for the \"Create\" and \"Join\" buttons were never attached to the page. I\'ve removed the duplicate declarations.\n- **Mock IRC API Payload**: The Express backend was previously returning `{ message: \"...\" }` for mock IRC commands, but the frontend code explicitly looks for `res.response`. This would have caused the script to throw another error upon joining a room. I\'ve updated the Express mock to return the correct payload structure.\n\nIf you click \"Create #channel\" or \"Join #channel\" now, the app\'s internal tab-routing engine successfully mounts the new channel as a distinct tab in the navigation bar, seamlessly hiding the Lobby and initializing the WebRTC/Chat interfaces!"
    modified_response: "I\'ve resolved the errors preventing the UI buttons from working. \n\n**Here is what was fixed:**\n- **JavaScript Syntax Errors**: During the migration, a duplicate declaration of the `sendIrcCommand` and `performIrcServiceCommands` functions slipped into `ivc.webrtc.js`. This caused a fatal syntax error that crashed the entire script, meaning the event listeners for the \"Create\" and \"Join\" buttons were never attached to the page. I\'ve removed the duplicate declarations.\n- **Mock IRC API Payload**: The Express backend was previously returning `{ message: \"...\" }` for mock IRC commands, but the frontend code explicitly looks for `res.response`. This would have caused the script to throw another error upon joining a room. I\'ve updated the Express mock to return the correct payload structure.\n\nIf you click \"Create #channel\" or \"Join #channel\" now, the app\'s internal tab-routing engine successfully mounts the new channel as a distinct tab in the navigation bar, seamlessly hiding the Lobby and initializing the WebRTC/Chat interfaces!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
